we've got some big news coming in today  in the fight to get back to normal  wouldn't that be great  amid this pandemic we're expecting  updated guidelines from the federal  government about  who should be wearing masks and when a  federal official tells cbs news that the  new cdc guidelines will lay out what  activities  fully vaccinated people may resume so  that includes when and  if it's necessary to continue wearing  the mask outdoors  currently cdc guidelines say the mass  may not be necessary outdoors if you're  away from  others or if you're only with people  from your household  also today president biden will give an  update on the state of the pandemic  a briefing from his covet 19 response  team will likely discuss  all of these new guidelines health and  human services secretary javier becerra  joins us now secretary becerra good  morning to you  we are at a crucial juncture uh in  combating covet 19  and we've got these new mass guidelines  coming down uh your department oversees  the cdc so i want to put the question to  you  first what we can expect and also it  sounds like it's going to be organized  around  whether or not a person is vaccinated or  not which i would read as a kind of  encouragement to get more people out  there  to get that vaccination fair to say yeah  good morning and thanks for having me  and absolutely uh the message is clear  you're vaccinated guess what you get to  return to a more normal lifestyle if  you're not vaccinated  you're still a danger you're still in  danger as well so get vaccinated  a cbs poll finds that while we are  making  improvements in the numbers of people  willing to get vaccinated there is still  a hardened core of about  between a quarter and a fifth of the  population saying  no way i know you're working on that  population but  what's your level of frustration that  we've reached a point where we may not  be able to make any more inroads  well remember when you get 130 million  americans fully vaccinated two-thirds of  all seniors today are fully vaccinated  that's all good news we want to build on  that we want others to join them  because when they join them being  vaccinated they can join them outside  and not have to wear masks secretary i  want to go back to the mass thing for  just a second because i've often  wondered  i'm outside by myself nobody's around  why am i wearing a mask  so this would be very helpful to know if  you're vaccinated  do you have to wear a mask outside or  you don't have to wear a mask outside  well we weren't born with masks but we  want to be safe and we want to protect  our loved ones  and so that's why we wear masks right we  put on our seat belt we don't expect  that we're going to crash our car  but we want to be safe that's what we're  just trying to do is make sure everyone  is safe  we want to get back to a normal  lifestyle we want to get our economy  going people back at work  restaurants open you got to do that the  right way and masks help  vaccinations important masks help and so  even though i'm  i've been vaccinated i still wear a mask  exactly so why do you why do we have to  do that if we're vaccinated that's why  i'm so confused  because i keep hearing you don't have to  wear it but still you could still  pass it or you could still pass it along  even though you've been vaccinated  that's why i'm confused yeah the vaccine  has done a really good job of making  sure  you'll not only be safe and healthy but  that you won't affect others but still  we you never know and what you're trying  to do is encourage others  we're going to get to a point where  masks we're going to hang or  hang up masks on our wall as as you know  signs of what used to be but until then  let's let's try to get to the point  where we're back to normal mr secretary  nearly 30 percent of covid cases are  among hispanics  and they make up less than 20 percent of  the population what's being done to get  the vaccine to the hispanic communities  oh great question because we're trying  to reach all those folks from who are in  hard-to-reach places and so many of the  workers  in america who were classified as  essential workers were latino  and so we're trying to get to them where  they are instead of  waiting for them to come to to the sites  where there's vaccinations opportunities  we're trying to go to them and that's  what we're doing throughout the country  we're doing that in rural areas because  we know a lot of americans  find it very difficult to get some of  these vaccination sites  we're going to go to where people are  we're going to make enough supply of  vaccinations  vaccines available and we're going to  make sure that we get everyone  vaccinated mr secretary i'd like to  shift topics  if we could to the border crisis there  are still record numbers of migrant  children unaccompanied arriving at the  u.s border  and where hhs comes into the picture is  after apprehension  the children are moved to a shelter and  then moved to a sponsor family the  shelter and the sponsor family that's  that's your department  uh how close are those shelters right  now to capacity  well pretty much at capacity and because  as you said they keep coming we keep  having to find more space  what we're trying to do is do this the  legal way the responsible way the right  way these are kids  and regardless of what their ultimate  outcome whether they're returned to  their home country  or not we have an obligation at hhs to  make sure we take care of their health  and their well-being while they're  temporarily with us mr secretary what do  you need  most right now to address that crisis do  you need more shelter space or do you  need more people to help you place these  kids with sponsor families  a little bit of both and uh what we're  finding is that we are  looking for as many of those places with  beds  that are licensed that have the  caregivers who are accustomed to  treating kids  and where we can't we still know it's  better to put them in our care  than keep them at the custom border  patrol centers because they're not  equipped to handle kids and so  we're going to do what's right by these  kids while they're temporarily with us  mr mr secretary the biden administration  does appear to be a little reluctant  to let the media cameras into these  facilities how come  well remember you're talking about  children these are not adults  they have privacy protections whether  you're an american citizen  or a migrant child seeking asylum you  have privacy protections you're not  you're not open to just the public to  identify you at the same time remember  covet still is out there and we can't  have people co-mingling  because we don't want to spread covet so  it's strictly a health issue and a  privacy issue  because some people say transparency  would help here  yeah oh we're all for that and we will  continue to open the sites  where it's possible when it's possible  when we can do it  reasonably but first and foremost safety  and well-being of those kids  privacy protections and making sure we  don't spread covet  all right secretary baser we appreciate  you getting up early for us this morning  thank you very much

